#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""nat-source-demo — a reference task-source plugin for nat, protocol v1.

The contract this implements is docs/design/task-sources/README.md
("Wire contract"). nat runs `nat-source-demo <method>` with exactly one JSON
object on stdin and reads exactly one JSON object from stdout; a non-zero
exit is an error, and the first non-empty stderr line is the message nat
shows.

Everything is fixed data except two files under the state directory
($XDG_STATE_HOME/nat-source-demo, else ~/.local/state/nat-source-demo):
events.log (one JSON line per `event`) and comments.json (comments added
through the composer, so they show on the next `container` read).

Standard library only, so it runs anywhere python3 does.
"""

